# R23 Wickermoor on the eve: the Round, the barricade, the bonfire, Dani, the retreat. By hand, polished by Gemini (R23 square), unvoiced.

~ arrive
Narrator: The Founder's Round has become a fortification run by people with no practice at it. Carts stand across the moor road, planks stand against the carts, and a long table is laid under lanterns in the inn yard. The goat is on the notice board.
set wv_square_seen
-> END

~ bonfire
Narrator: Above the houses to the north the bonfire on the hill burns without moving. Smoke goes up off the moor in a single, patient column. Everyone in the Round has looked at it so often they have stopped seeing it.
set wv_bonfire_watched
-> END

~ barricade
Narrator: A line of carts, planks and a fence dragged across the moor road mouth. It would stop a calf.
* [Athletics DC 14] Haul the carts into a proper line -> barr_ok | barr_fail
* [Investigation DC 14] Find the weak joints and brace them -> barr_ok | barr_fail
* Ask the militia to do it properly -> barr_ask
* Leave it -> END

~ barr_ok
Narrator: The barricade stands taller, and a gap is left where a person can walk through and a cart cannot.
set wv_barricade_built
temp_hp 2d8 party
-> END

~ barr_fail
Narrator: A cart rolls back on its wheel and takes you with it. You are sore, and it is still a cart.
damage 1d6 bludgeoning
-> END

~ barr_ask
Narrator: The volunteers form a bucket line, and then, by degrees, a barricade. It is not elegant. It is up.
set wv_barricade_built
-> END

~ dani
dani_jenkin [neutral]: The village is more afraid of the fire than of the wicker. The wicker will walk. I have seen it. Stay as long as you want. It will not be long.
-> END

~ retreat_confirm
Narrator: To go back is to leave the moor to the fire. The cult will burn everyone who is chained there, and the Wicker Man will walk down at full power to the village.
* Fall back to the village and make a stand there -> retreat_go
* Stay and fight on -> END

~ retreat_go
Narrator: You turn your back on the hill, and the hymn on it swells as if it were glad of you.
set vigil_fled
set vigil_deaths += 6
quest wickers_vigil fallen_back
move wv_square:from_moors

~ fall_back_gate
Narrator: The barricade holds, for now, and the whole Round has gone quiet. Every eye is on the north road, and the road is empty. Then the ground begins to shake, and the lanterns on their poles begin to sway.
Narrator: A shape of willow, taller than the church, comes out of the dark in the red of its own fire.
crooked_man [sly]: Nobody home on the hill? Fine. I shall call on you!
-> fall_back_menu

~ fall_back_menu
* Hold the Round against it -> square_fight
* Run, and leave the village to the fire -> abandon

~ square_fight
Narrator: The first slam brings down a house.
combat wv_wicker_square

~ abandon
Narrator: You take the south road. Behind you the lanterns go out, one at a time, and then the houses.
set wicker_man_triumphant
quest wickers_vigil ash_over_the_hollow
end_game
